The Public Health (Tobacco Products and Nicotine Inhaling Products) (Amendment) Bill 2026 has been signed into law by Uachtarán na hÉireann. Together with the Public Health (Single-Use Vapes) Act 2026, this legislation aims to reduce the appeal and accessibility of vapes and other nicotine products to young people.
The Act will introduce a range of measures, including:
• Prohibiting the sale of nicotine consumption products such as nicotine pouches to people under 18;
• Prohibiting the advertising of nicotine inhaling products and nicotine consumption products in retail outlets as well as their point-of-sale display in mixed retail outlets;
• Restricting colours and imagery used on nicotine inhaling products their packaging;
• Prohibiting the sale of devices resembling or functioning as other products, such as toys or games; and
• Prohibiting flavour names for nicotine inhaling products to "Tobacco" and "Unflavoured", with powers to amend this list by regulation.

