• the role of data centres as critical digital infrastructure, underpinning significant levels of economic activity across many sectors of the Irish economy. For 2024, the study estimates that data centres located in Ireland enabled economic activity on the scale of approximately €104 billion in Gross Value Added (GVA) (approximately 20% of the national total) was enabled by data centres located in Ireland across the country's six most data centre-dependent sectors;
• their role in reinforcing Ireland's attractiveness for global technology investment and underpinning Ireland's internationally significant computer services exports by foreign-owned firms, which reached €262 billion in 2024 and accounted for over half of total services exports;
